a demon and brother of Rāvaṇa. [Though a demon by birth, he was extremely sorry for the abduction of Sītā by Rāvaṇa, and severely reprimanded him for his wicked act. He several times advised Rāvaṇa to restore Sītā to Rāma if he cared to live; but the proud demon turned a deaf ear to his warnings. At last seeing that the ruin of his brother was inevitable, he repaired to Rāma and became his staunch friend. After the death of Rāvaṇa, Rāma installed him on the throne of Laṅkā. He is believed to be one of the seven Chirajīvins; see चिरजीविन्.]", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bibhiiShaNa", "bibhīṣaṇa"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bibhiiShaNa", "bibhīṣaṇa"]}], "biBisika": [{"id": "biBIzikA", "headword": "बिभीषिका", "headword_slp1": "biBIzikA", "fold": "biBisika", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "बिभीषिका [bibhīṣikā], 1 Threatening, terror.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "That which threatens or scares away; यदि ते सन्ति सन्त्वेव केयमन्या बिभीषिका U.4.29. See बिभीषिका.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bibhiiShikaa", "bibhīṣikā"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bibhiiShikaa", "bibhīṣikā"]}], "biBraksu": [{"id": "biBrakzu", "headword": "बिभ्रक्षु", "headword_slp1": "biBrakzu", "fold": "biBraksu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "बिभ्रक्षु [bibhrakṣu], a.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Wishing to roast or fry.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Desirous of scorching up.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Wishing to destroy. -क्षुः Fire.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bibhrakṣu", "bibhraxu"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bibhrakṣu", "bibhraxu"]}], "biBrajisu": [{"id": "biBrajjizu", "headword": "बिभ्रज्जिषु", "headword_slp1": "biBrajjizu", "fold": "biBrajisu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "बिभ्रज्जिषु [bibhrajjiṣu], a. Wishing to fry. -षुः Fire; रुषा बिभ्रज्जिषु- प्रख्यं कपिं बाणैरवाकिरत् Bk.9.34.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bibhrajjiShu", "bibhrajjiṣu"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bibhrajjiShu", "bibhrajjiṣu"]}], "biBatsa": [{"id": "bIBatsa", "headword": "बीभत्स", "headword_slp1": "bIBatsa", "fold": "biBatsa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "बीभत्स [bībhatsa], a. [बध् स्वार्थे सन्]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Disgusting, loathsome. nauseous, hideous, revolting; हन्त बीभत्समेवाग्रे वर्तते Māl. 5 'Oh ! it is indeed a loathsome sight'.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Envious, malignant, mischievous.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Savage, cruel, ferocious.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Estranged in mind.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Loathing, detesting; बीभत्सु- रतिबीभत्सं कर्मेदमकरोत् कथम् Mb.11.24.13.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Sinful, wicked.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "त्सः Disgust, abhorrence, detestation.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "The disgusting sentiment, one of the 8 or 9 rasas in poetry; जुगुप्सास्थायिभावस्तु बीभत्सः कथ्यते रसः S. D.236. (e. g. Māl.5.16.).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of Arjuna. -त्सा Loathing, abhorrence. -त्सम् Anything loathsome.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["biibhatsa", "bībhatsa"], "synonyms_slp1": ["biibhatsa", "bībhatsa"]}], "biBatsu": [{"id": "bIBatsu", "headword": "बीभत्सु", "headword_slp1": "bIBatsu", "fold": "biBatsu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "बीभत्सु [bībhatsu], a. Loathing, abhorring, detesting.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Disgusted.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Reserved, coy (said of a woman); सा बीभत्सुर्गर्भरसा निविद्धा Rv.1.164.8. -त्सुः an epithet of Arjuna; (Mb. thus explains the word: न कुर्यां कर्म बीभत्सं युध्यमानः कथंचन । तेन देवमनुष्येषु बीभत्सुरिति विश्रुतः ॥); तृट्परितः परिशान्तो बीभत्सुर्यमुनामगात् Bhāg.1.58.16.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["biibhatsu", "bībhatsu"], "synonyms_slp1": ["biibhatsu", "bībhatsu"]}]}